+# Capture correction r2: prepared only
+
+Original stage and PINS are unchanged. baseline/ preserves every original pinned file; PRIOR-PINS.json preserves its manifest. Actual original remote program was7676bytes, below the common8192byte pipe capacity. No stall was reproduced. The defects are synchronous stdin write before entering the deadline loop (allowed input up to32768bytes), and missing finally cleanup if stdin/selector operations fail.
+
+The corrected common routine uses unbuffered pipes and nonblocking stdin registered for selector WRITE alongside stdout/stderr READ. Partial os.write advances an offset; EAGAIN/EINTR retry within the unchanged deadline; stdin closes when all bytes are sent. BrokenPipe records the error but continues draining diagnostic streams within that deadline. Other exceptions retain captured bounded prefixes and enter finally. Output caps apply in normal and fallback drains. Original metadata queries, caps and command deadlines are unchanged.
+
+No poll()/wait() reaps the child before cleanup. waitid(WNOWAIT) checks state while keeping its PID reserved. This capture routine is the sole reaper of its Popen child. Finally confirms that relationship before signaling only the new session/process group it created; if ownership was lost it sends no group signal and reports an error. It drains immediately available diagnostics without blocking, closes streams/selector, then waits up to2seconds for its child. Cleanup errors remain in the result. Neither child reaping nor local group signaling proves remote death or complete group disappearance: both proof fields stay false and root independently collects the same scope. Outer runtime/resource guard remains the bound if process creation/kernel operations stall or external termination prevents Python finally.
+
+No source module imported or executed, no functional test, subprocess fixture, SSH contact or live action performed. Python syntax checked by AST only. This is a reviewable source correction, not a tested runtime claim. Root must inspect CAPTURE-R2.patch and the updated pins before one read admission. No ROOT-ADMISSION/ATTEMPT/RESULT exists in this revision.
